GamerWiki extensions
====================

Bundled (always on)
-------------------

These are part of GamerWiki. They are loaded by includes/DefaultSettings.php
($wgGamerWikiBundledExtensions), need no line in LocalSettings.php, and
are not offered by the installer. They are the versions made for
MediaWiki 1.19 (2012-2014), fixed to run on PHP 8, with their optional
JavaScript removed.

  Extension               Version used              License
  ----------------------  ------------------------  ------------------------
  ParserFunctions         REL1_19 (1.4.1)           GPL-2.0-or-later
  Cite (+ Special:Cite)   REL1_19                   GPL-2.0-or-later
  CharInsert              REL1_19                   GPL-2.0-or-later
  ImageMap                REL1_19                   GPL-2.0-or-later
  InputBox                REL1_19                   Public domain
  Poem                    REL1_19                   Permissive ("any purpose")
  Interwiki               REL1_19                   GPL-2.0-or-later
  Nuke                    REL1_19                   GPL-2.0-or-later
  Renameuser              REL1_19                   GPL-2.0-or-later
  ReplaceText             0.9.5                     GPL-2.0-or-later
  SyntaxHighlight_GeSHi   REL1_19 + GeSHi 1.0.8.10  GPL-2.0-or-later
  PdfHandler              REL1_19                   GPL-2.0-or-later
  DPLforum                REL1_21                   GPL-2.0-or-later
  Variables               REL1_21                   ISC
  Loops                   REL1_21                   GPL-2.0-or-later
  WikiSEO                 1.2.0                     GPL-2.0-or-later

All of these licenses allow the code to be distributed as part of
GamerWiki under the GNU GPL version 2 or later (see COPYING).

GamerWiki changes to them: PHP 8 fixes (constructors, create_function,
pass-by-reference parser arguments, newer-MediaWiki calls in WikiSEO), an
edit-token check on Special:ReplaceText, and removal of Cite's reference
popups and ReplaceText's "invert selection" button (both JavaScript).

PdfHandler draws PDF thumbnails with Ghostscript ("gs") and reads PDF text
with pdfinfo/pdftotext (poppler-utils). Without them, PDFs still upload and
link, just without a preview.

Also built into core instead of bundled: __DISAMBIG__ (Disambiguator) and
__EXPECTUNUSEDCATEGORY__.

Left out on purpose
-------------------

  Scribunto (Lua), TimedMediaHandler, Math (needs texvc, LaTeX and dvipng),
  PageImages and TextExtracts (API-only), and every skin except MonoBook.

Optional
--------

ConfirmEdit (CAPTCHAs), Gadgets (user JavaScript/CSS gadgets) and
WikiEditor (the JavaScript editing toolbar) ship in this directory but are
off unless you enable them in the installer or with a require_once line in
LocalSettings.php. Other 1.19-compatible extensions can be added the same
way: put them in a folder here and follow their install instructions.
